course: dictionary
lesson: 11330
title: Vocabulary in context: yolk
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are easy to picture, and context helps you check what they mean. «An egg has a yellow yolk, the food store for a chick, and a clear white that cushions it.» The sentence tells you the yolk is inside the egg and that it is food. So yolk must be the yellow part in the middle.
explain: Context can also show you a job a word does. «Separate the yolk from the white» means you split them apart. In a recipe, you would not separate things that are already mixed, so the words around yolk tell you it is a separate part of the egg.
explain: Some words look like they belong to one meaning, but the context shows a second meaning. «Some sharks and skates lay eggs in tough cases called mermaid's purses, and the baby grows inside, fed by a yolk.» Here the yolk is not for breakfast. It is the food store that feeds a baby animal while it grows.
fact: The yolk is the round yellow or orange part in the middle of an egg.
fact: In science, the yolk is the food store for a growing baby bird or other animal inside the egg.
fact: «Runny yolk» means a soft yolk that flows, as in a soft-boiled egg.
fact: In cooking, yolks and whites are often separated, for example for cakes and custard.
fact: Always wash your hands after touching raw eggs.
exercise: «An egg has a yellow yolk, the food store for a chick.» What is the yolk for? | To make the shell hard | To hold the feathers together | *To feed a growing chick | To keep the egg cold
exercise: In a recipe, you are told to «separate the yolk from the white». What does separate mean? | Cover with a lid | Heat up | Mix together | *Split apart
exercise: «A runny yolk is soft-boiled.» What does runny suggest about the yolk? | *Soft and flowing | Green all the way through | Hard and crunchy | Cold and frozen
test: «Double-yolk eggs come most often from young hens whose egg-making has not settled, so two yolks are released at once.» What is a double-yolk egg? | An egg with a blue shell | An egg with no white | A boiled egg cut in half | *An egg with two yolks
test: «Some sharks and skates lay eggs in tough cases called mermaid's purses, and the baby grows inside, fed by a yolk.» Why does the baby grow inside the case? | It is fed by the mother's milk | It eats the case | It sleeps all the time | *It is fed by the yolk
exam: Why should you wash your hands after touching raw eggs? | To make the white whiter | To make the yolk yellower | Because eggs are heavy | *For safety
